🧟 Mercury Master Commands Cheat Sheet
​To start your server from scratch, first download your folder and run the master installer:
chmod +x masterinstaller.sh && ./masterinstaller.sh
(Note: The system will automatically reboot after completion.)  
​🕹️ The "m" Master Interface
​Once installed, use these single-letter commands for daily management:  
​m up: Starts all media apps in the background.  
​m status: Dashboard view of storage, GPU temperature, and container health.  
​m gpu: Live 1-second monitor for GTX 750 usage and performance.  
​m ps: Shows exactly which apps are running and their network ports.  
​m reset: The "Nuclear" option—wipes cache and restarts the entire stack fresh.  
​m mount: Refreshes and remounts your "Vault" expansion drive.  
​m urls: Displays the local IP links for all your Web UIs.
​📂 Quick File Paths
​Blueprint: ~/mercury/docker-compose.yml  
​Vault: /media/linux/Expansion  
​Configs: ~/mercury/config/  
